    {
      "element_id": "prisma_2020_9_e6",
      "status": "NOT_APPLICABLE",
      "chunk_id": "text_8",
      "quote": "The search strategy used a combination of the MeSH terms 'preterm' or 'stillbirth' AND 'Covid19' or 'SARS-­ CoV-­ 2' and included any type of study design published in the English language (Appendix S1).",
      "reason": "Only English-language publications were included, so no translation of articles for data collection was required, making this conditional requirement inapplicable."
    },
    {
      "element_id": "prisma_2020_9_e7",
      "status": "NOT_APPLICABLE",
      "chunk_id": "text_11",
      "quote": "The information extracted included details of the publication, study setting and size, pre-­ pandemic period definition, pandemic period definition, and rates of the reported outcomes in pre-­ pandemic and pandemic time periods.",
      "reason": "Data extraction is described only for published study details and reported outcome rates; there is no indication that data were extracted from figures, so specification of figure-extraction software does not apply."
    },
    {
      "element_id": "prisma_2020_9_e8",
      "status": "PRESENT",
      "chunk_id": "text_13",
      "quote": "Khalil et al 9 had overlapping data for stillbirth outcome with another study; however, preterm birth data were not overlapping, so only preterm birth data were used in this review.",
      "reason": "Decision rules for selecting data from multiple/overlapping reports are described, including use of only non-overlapping preterm birth data from Khalil et al, replacement of Simpson et al with the larger Shah et al dataset, and extraction of Canadian data excluding Ontario from Liu et al to avoid double counting."
    }
  ],
  "confidence": 88
}

{
