{
  "item_id": "PRISMA_2020_13a",
  "elements": [
    {
      "element_id": "prisma_2020_13a_e1",
      "status": "PARTIAL",
      "chunk_id": "text_13",
      "quote": "For one study conducted in the Netherlands by Been et al, 54 data were presented using multiple cut-­ offs to define the pre-­ and post-­ pandemic periods... we, therefore, included this study in the systematic review but not in meta-­ analyses. Khalil et al 9 had overlapping data for stillbirth outcome with another study; however, preterm birth data were not overlapping, so only preterm birth data were used in this review.",
      "reason": "The manuscript partially describes processes for deciding study eligibility for each synthesis: general eligibility criteria are in text_8 ('Studies were included if they compared pregnancy outcomes between the COVID-19 pandemic period and pre-pandemic time periods and reported on any of the outcomes of interest'), and text_13 explains study-specific decisions about inclusion in the review vs meta-analyses (e.g., Been et al excluded from meta-analyses, overlapping data handling, replacing Simpson et al with Shah et al). text_12 also notes meta-analyses were planned for studies with similar outcomes and methodological homogeneity. However, no systematic process (e.g., tabulating study characteristics against planned synthesis groups) is described, so the description is incomplete."
    }
  ],
  "confidence": 78
}

